Found during k96 (worker). In the published layout, an agents/ or rules/ dir holding both x.md and x.md.njk yields two catalog items named x (skills cannot: one dir per name). The .claude/ scan dedupes (sorted, x.md wins). Expected: one item, or a clear catalog error naming both files – decide which, consistent with bundles (both .yaml and .yml is an error of that bundle).

2026-09-27 00:28 Decision (maintainer, 2026-09-27): catalog error naming both files, consistent with bundles (.yaml + .yml). The .claude/ scan keeps its dedupe.

2026-09-27 01:13 Scope decision: the error belongs to that one item (type + name), never to the scan – mirroring the bundle clash (scanBundles keeps the bundle in cat.bundles with error instead of def; spec §15.4 'affect only the bundle concerned'). Shape: the item stays in cat.items once, with files = both paths and error = 'both agents/x.md and agents/x.md.njk exist' (same wording as the bundle's). Consequences: scan never throws for it; every other item (incl. a same-named item of another type) is unaffected; a .claude/ item of that name is still skipped (the published layout found the name first); sync (explicit, wildcard, bundle) warns naming both files and keeps an installed copy, like a template error / unresolvable item; install fails before editing, like checkBundle; available lists it once with its error (text: an 'error:' line, --json: an error field, as bundles). The .claude/ scan dedupe is unchanged.

